WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.720
Wong – like, Adele? As of "Spider-Man: No&nbsp;
Way Home," it's more like "Sorcerer Supreme."&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.920
Tom Holland's Spider-Man is unlike&nbsp;
anything we've seen before from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:14.320
web-slinger on the big screen. In earlier&nbsp;
movies, Peter Parker often acted as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.120
lone wolf. He worked by himself and never seemed&nbsp;
to encounter other superheroes in his world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:23.440
even in New York City, home to most of&nbsp;
the Marvel universe's superheroes. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:28.000
changed pretty drastically with the character's&nbsp;
introduction into the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.480
where he has had plenty of opportunities to&nbsp;
fight alongside Earth's mightiest heroes.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:36.400
"Cap'n. Big fan. Spider-Man."

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.360
"Yeah, we'll talk about it later."

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:38.720
"Hey everyone."

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:39.120
"Good job."

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.880
In "Captain America: Civil War" and "Spider-Man:&nbsp;
Homecoming," he was a protégé of Iron Man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.120
In "Spider-Man: Far From Home," he had to&nbsp;
try to live up to Tony Stark's expectations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.760
in the aftermath of Iron Man's death. And, in&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: No Way Home," Peter turns to a member&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.960
of his old "Avengers: Infinity War" cohort,&nbsp;
Doctor Strange, to help him out of a pinch.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.480
As "No Way Home" begins, Peter's dealing&nbsp;
with the ramifications of having his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.520
identity exposed to the world. He turns&nbsp;
to the Bleecker Street sorcerer to cast a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.760
spell so that no one will remember that Peter&nbsp;
Parker and Spider-Man are one and the same.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.000
It's at this moment we get an intriguing&nbsp;
new bit of information about a key player,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.600
and it's something every MCU fan&nbsp;
maybe should have seen coming.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.640
After Peter shows up, Doctor Strange and Wong&nbsp;
discuss the ethical and practical ramifications&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:29.360
of casting a spell that will impact everyone&nbsp;
on the planet, including themselves. It's at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.720
this point Wong makes it known he is now the&nbsp;
Sorcerer Supreme, and it makes total sense.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.920
In "Infinity War," Wong is left to protect&nbsp;
the Sanctum Sanctorum when Ebony Maw takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.720
Strange prisoner. While the movie makes it&nbsp;
unclear if Wong is a casualty of The Blip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:50.400
the actor who plays him, Benedict Wong, confirmed&nbsp;
in a 2019 Reddit AMA that he would likely take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.320
over as Sorcerer Supreme. Although Strange&nbsp;
was originally tapped to hold the title,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:59.440
he was gone for five years, courtesy of Thanos.&nbsp;
Naturally, the title had to go to someone else,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.480
considering everyone thought&nbsp;
Strange was permanently dead.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.400
The revelation about Wong's new status&nbsp;
within the sorcerer hierarchy provides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.320
new context to an exchange featured&nbsp;
in the "No Way Home" teaser trailer:

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.200
"Don't cast that spell. It's too dangerous."

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.680
"Fine. I won't."

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.800
We now know that order isn't coming from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.560
a peer. it's coming from someone&nbsp;
who's effectively Strange's boss.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.360
What does this mean for the future of the&nbsp;
MCU? Probably not much. Doctor Strange still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.000
has full control of his powers, including his&nbsp;
ability to manipulate reality per his whims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.480
Wong will likely still be Sorcerer Supreme&nbsp;
going into "Doctor Strange in the Multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.040
of Madness," but that likely won't stop&nbsp;
Strange from messing with other realities and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.720
interacting with Scarlet Witch along&nbsp;
the way. It's simply a title change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.480
though it's one that Wong probably&nbsp;
won't want to give up any time soon.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.800
Wong as the Sorcerer Supreme makes sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.560
but one aspect of his new role that may&nbsp;
have fans scratching their heads is why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.200
such a powerful individual spends their&nbsp;
time fighting in underground cage fights.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.200
As Marvel fans will remember, Wong&nbsp;
was part of Xialing's superpowered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.080
tournament in "Shang-Chi and&nbsp;
the Legend of the Ten Rings."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:10.160
Such an act might make sense for a sorcerer&nbsp;
who's short on rent money for the month.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.320
But doesn't the Sorcerer Supreme have better&nbsp;
things to do than break The Abomination out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.560
of a high-security prison to battle him in&nbsp;
front of a bunch of spectators and gamblers?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.080
Maybe Wong just loves the thrill of the&nbsp;
fight. Perhaps he's having trouble paying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:24.800
off the homeowner's tax for the Sanctum Sanctorum.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:28.880
It's undoubtedly expensive right smack dab&nbsp;
in the middle of Manhattan. Either way, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.280
appears that Doctor Strange isn't the only wizard&nbsp;
who's willing to bend the rules a little bit.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.560
The real question remains whether Wong will retain&nbsp;
the title of Sorcerer Supreme or if Strange will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:43.040
take it back at some point in "Doctor Strange&nbsp;
in the Multiverse of Madness." Time will tell.

